s":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":13,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"reviewer\":\"numerical_auditor\",\"paper_id\":\"bicycle-infrastructure-paper\",\"run_status\":\"ok\",\"summary\":\"Most reported figures recompute: the pilot funnel (70 hits, 36 duplicates, 34 unique), the 2x2 agreement tables (33/34 = 97%), the Table 6 project precision breakdown (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the Table 8 listing counts and shares, the Table 8 type shares against Figure 2 word shares (bounds only), and the Figure 4 county values against the text. Two verifiable defects were found. (1) The pilot yield \\\"2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)\\\" uses a count of distinct openings (2) against a count of articles (34), while the paper's own article-level count of articles coded relevant is 5. (2) Footnote 3 says the Stord article was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 shows the second coder with 4 relevant articles against 3 for the pilot coder, and the text identifies the one disagreement article as the Stord article. Two further items cannot be resolved numerically from retained artifacts: whether the Appendix A.3.2 \\\"first type in the table\\\" rule is consistent with the bysykkelstativ and syklende assignments in Table 9 and Figure 2 and how this affects Table 8 type shares; and how the plotted Q2 2024 point in Figure 3 was computed, given that the stated gap runs January to April 2024 while the text says only the first quarter is missing. Table CSV/markdown extraction is unreliable per parser-quality guidance, so table numbers were read from page text and retained images.\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"NUM-001\",\"category\":\"percentage_denominator_unit_mismatch\",\"finding_summary\":\"The pilot yield 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place' uses a count of distinct openings (2) as the numerator over a count of articles (34); the paper's own article-level count of articles coded relevant is 5 of 34.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"confidence\":\"high\",\"location\":{\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Pilot sample\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Figure 1 (page 4) lists 34 unique articles, 5 coded 'relevant' (15% retained) and 2 'Distinct openings that took place'. Section 3.1.4 states 'Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.' (four Homborsund articles and one Stod). The numerator 2 therefore counts projects/openings, while the denominator 34 counts articles. In article units the paper's own count is 5 of 34 (14.7%, shown as 15% in Figure 1), or 3 of 34 (8.8%) after the validation recode of the two pre-opening Homborsund articles (Section 3.1.4). The statement that 2 openings were found is consistent with the data; the article-level share is not. The Figure 1 caption 'Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening' has the same unit mix, but the caption is not separately numerically assessed here. Whether the sentence is meant to refer to articles or openings is not stated.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2\",\"text_quote\":\"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 5 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md\",\"page\":5,\"page_label\":\"5\",\"section\":\"3.1.4\",\"text_quote\":\"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":null},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 4 Figure 1 labels\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md\",\"page\":4,\"page_label\":\"4\",\"section\":\"3.1.2 Figure 1\",\"text_quote\":\"Coded “relevant” 5 15 % retained\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Figure 1 chart labels are retained in the page-4 text; the figure_1.png crop omits the chart, so the page text was used.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"2 of 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"The numerator counts openings; the paper's article count coded relevant is 5 (3 after the validation recode).\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"2\",\"source_id\":\"S1\",\"unit\":\"articles (as worded in the sentence)\",\"sample\":\"pilot sample, 34 unique articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Numerator in 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles'; the same number is the count of distinct openings in Figure 1 and Section 3.1.4\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"5\",\"source_id\":\"S3\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"pilot sample, 34 unique articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Figure 1 'Coded relevant' count of articles (four Homborsund and one Stod per Section 3.1.4)\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Same 34 unique pilot articles. The 5 counts articles coded relevant; the 2 counts distinct openings that took place. The sentence applies the openings count to an article denominator. The article-level count after the validation recode (3) is stated in Section 3.1.4, but the paper does not say which version the sentence intends.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"Stated numerator 2 'articles' versus 5 articles coded relevant in the same 34-article sample (3 after the validation recode); the stated 6% (2/34 = 5.9%) corresponds to openings, not articles. 5/34 = 14.7%; 3/34 = 8.8%.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The authors may have intended an opening-level statement and used the article denominator, or may have intended articles that report an opening that actually took place before the validation recode.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State the yield in one unit, either articles (5 of 34, or 3 of 34 after the validation recode, specifying which) or openings (2 distinct openings), and align the Figure 1 caption.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Restate the pilot yield in a single unit (articles or openings) and state which article count (5 or 3) is intended; align the Figure 1 caption.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-002\",\"category\":\"cross_source_count_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"Footnote 3 says the Stord article was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 shows 4 relevant articles for the second coder against 3 for the pilot coder, and the text says the only disagreement article is the Stord article.\",\"issue_type\":\"manuscript_issue\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)\",\"text_quote\":\"was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4)\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The 44 projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).\",\"assessment\":\"no\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":null,\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 3 (second coder in columns) has pilot-coder rows 'Relevant 3 0 3' and 'Not relevant 1 30 31', and column totals 'Total 4 30 34'; the pilot coder has 3 relevant articles and the second coder 4. The only off-diagonal cell is pilot coder 'Not relevant' and second coder 'Relevant'. The Section 4.1 text says 'The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County'. If the Stord article is that article, one coder coded it relevant, which conflicts with footnote 3 saying both coded it not relevant. The retained text does not say which coder gave which code, nor whether the footnote's Stord project is the same article as the Section 4.1 disagreement article (the Stord article in the disagreement is a dispute article, not an opening article); the check relies on the table cell structure and the text. Table 3 body cells were compared with table_3.png by the parser audit and match.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 10 footnote 3\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md\",\"page\":10,\"page_label\":\"10\",\"section\":\"6\",\"text_quote\":\"was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4)\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Footnote text is split across two lines in the extraction.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 Table 3 totals\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1 / Table 3\",\"text_quote\":\"Total 4 30 34\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 3 read from page text because the table markdown has a merged header.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 text on the disagreement\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4.1\",\"text_quote\":\"The only article they disagree on covers a\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"The sentence continues on the next line: 'dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County'.\"},{\"id\":\"S4\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 7 pilot coder relevant count\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md\",\"page\":7,\"page_label\":\"7\",\"section\":\"4\",\"text_quote\":\"of which 3 were coded as relevant in the pilot\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"A footnote marker is attached to 'pilot' in the extraction and is not part of the quote.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Stord article coded not relevant by both human coders\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\",\"S4\"],\"relation\":\"contradicts\",\"note\":\"Table 3 gives the second coder one more relevant article than the pilot coder, and the text identifies the one disagreement article as the Stord article.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"cross_source\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"3\",\"source_id\":\"S4\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Number of articles the pilot coder coded relevant (Table 3 row 'Relevant 3 0 3')\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"},{\"value\":\"4\",\"source_id\":\"S2\",\"unit\":\"articles\",\"sample\":\"34 unique pilot articles\",\"denominator\":\"34 unique articles\",\"context\":\"Number of articles the second coder coded relevant (Table 3 'Total 4 30 34'); 'unclear' counted as not relevant per the Table 3 note\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0\",\"scale\":\"number\"}],\"comparability\":\"Both counts refer to the same 34 pilot articles and the same relevance coding. Footnote 3 prints no number; it implies that neither coder coded the Stord article relevant, in which case the second coder's relevant count would not exceed the pilot coder's. That the disagreement article is the Stord article of footnote 3 is taken from the Section 4.1 text.\",\"observed_discrepancy\":\"The second coder has 4 relevant articles and the pilot coder 3; the one disagreement article is described as the Stord article, whereas footnote 3 says both coders coded the Stord article not relevant.\",\"possible_explanation\":\"The footnote may refer to a different Stord article or to the pilot coder only, or may reflect a later recode. The retained text does not say.\",\"suggested_correction\":\"State which coder coded the Stord article as relevant and reconcile footnote 3 with Table 3, or clarify which Stord article the footnote refers to.\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Reconcile footnote 3 with Table 3 and the Section 4.1 text, stating which coder (and the LLM) classified the Stord article as relevant.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-003\",\"category\":\"classification_rule_vs_reported_shares\",\"finding_summary\":\"The Appendix A.3.2 rule 'given the first type in the table' does not obviously produce the bysykkelstativ and syklende assignments shown in the text, Table 9 and Figure 2; whether this changes the Table 8 type shares cannot be computed from retained artifacts.\",\"issue_type\":\"cannot_verify\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions\",\"text_quote\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing “bysykkel” (city bike), such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"The retained artifacts do not contain the implemented classification order or any manual override, nor listing-level overlaps between words, so the effect of the apparent rule conflict on the Table 8 type shares cannot be computed.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"Table 9 orders the types 'The word “bicycle”', Proximity, Parking & storage, Leisure, Infrastructure, Other. 'Parking & storage' includes 'stativ' (rack), so 'bysykkelstativ' contains a Parking & storage part that precedes Infrastructure, yet the text says it is counted as infrastructure and Figure 2 colours bysykkelstativ (0.5%) blue (Infrastructure), while sykkelstativ (1.2%) is orange (Parking & storage). 'syklende' (0.3%) is listed under Infrastructure and coloured blue although it contains 'sykle', a Proximity part listed earlier. The example for bysykkel may be an explicit override rather than a literal first-type outcome, which the text does not say. Table 8 reports listing-level any-word type shares, so the effect of reclassifying one or two words (each at most 0.5% and 0.3% of listings) cannot be derived from the retained evidence. The Table 8 type shares are within the bounds implied by Figure 2 word shares.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 18 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md\",\"page\":18,\"page_label\":\"18\",\"section\":\"A.3.2\",\"text_quote\":\"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 9 rows read from page text because table_9.md is unstructured per parser quality.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"figure_2.png\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_2.png\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 2\",\"text_quote\":null,\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-be07133eb1a3ae76638fe011\",\"correspondence\":\"visual\",\"verification_note\":\"Figure 2 viewed. Bars for bysykkelstativ (0.5%) and syklende (0.3%) are in the Infrastructure colour; sykkelstativ is in the Parking & storage colour; sykle is in the Proximity colour.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 15 Table 8 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md\",\"page\":15,\"page_label\":\"15\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Table 8\",\"text_quote\":\"Infrastructure 93 786 13.4%\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Table 8 read from page text, not the split CSV columns.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"First-type rule determines the type of each word\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"Two assignments do not follow a literal reading of the stated precedence.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Do the reported Table 8 type shares (for example Infrastructure 13.4% of 700 579 listings) follow the stated first-type rule, or would reclassifying bysykkelstativ and syklende change them?\",\"quantities\":[{\"value\":\"13.4\",\"source_id\":\"S3\",\"unit\":\"percent of all listings\",\"sample\":\"700 579 FINN.no listings, January 2020 to October 2026\",\"denominator\":\"700 579 listings\",\"context\":\"Table 8 Infrastructure share, quoted for context only; no recomputation of the type shares under an alternative classification is possible\",\"rounding_half_width\":\"0.05\",\"scale\":\"percent\"}],\"missing_information\":[\"Listing-level overlap between words, since a listing can contain several word types\",\"The classification order actually implemented and any manual overrides\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"State the actual precedence or the override applied (for example whether 'bysykkel' words are classified before 'stativ'), and confirm that Table 8 and Figure 2 use the same assignment.\"},{\"id\":\"NUM-004\",\"category\":\"timing_gap_inconsistency\",\"finding_summary\":\"The text says only the first quarter of 2024 is missing, but the stated data gap is January to April 2024, which reaches into Q2, and Figure 3 plots a Q2 2024 point without saying how it was computed.\",\"issue_type\":\"cannot_verify\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"confidence\":\"medium\",\"location\":{\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 3\",\"text_quote\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"precision\":\"exact\"},\"claim_text\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"assessment\":\"cannot_verify\",\"cannot_verify_reason\":\"The retained artifacts do not state how the Q2 2024 point in Figure 3 was constructed (partial quarter, only May and June listings, or another treatment), and the underlying quarterly series is not available, so the effect of the partial gap on the plotted share cannot be assessed.\",\"evidence_summary\":\"Appendix A.1 states 'Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data' and the Figure 3 caption says 'missing listing text from January to April 2024'. Four months extends one month beyond Q1. The page-16 sentence says only the first quarter is missing. In the Figure 3 image the last pre-gap point sits at about 2023.75 (Q4 2023, about 34%) and the first post-gap point (about 39%) at about 2024.25, so a Q2 2024 point is plotted. If April is missing, that point may rest on May and June only and may not be comparable with full-quarter points; the text does not say. The text's rise from about 35 percent to about 44 percent is consistent with the plotted endpoints.\",\"source_objects\":[{\"id\":\"S1\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 16 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2\",\"text_quote\":\"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Sentence is split across two lines in the extraction.\"},{\"id\":\"S2\",\"type\":\"text\",\"label\":\"page 15 text\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md\",\"page\":15,\"page_label\":\"15\",\"section\":\"A.1\",\"text_quote\":\"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.\",\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f\",\"correspondence\":\"text\",\"verification_note\":\"Sentence is split across two lines in the extraction.\"},{\"id\":\"S3\",\"type\":\"figure\",\"label\":\"figure_3.png\",\"path\":\"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_3.png\",\"page\":16,\"page_label\":\"16\",\"section\":\"A.2 / Figure 3\",\"text_quote\":null,\"url\":null,\"object_id\":\"OBJ-22f18338a427285653860df1\",\"correspondence\":\"visual\",\"verification_note\":\"Figure 3 viewed. No point between about 2023.75 and about 2024.25; the first post-gap point sits at about 2024.25 (Q2 2024). Point positions and values are read visually and are approximate.\"}],\"claim_evidence_links\":[{\"claim_text\":\"Only the first quarter of 2024 is missing\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"S1\",\"S2\",\"S3\"],\"relation\":\"partial\",\"note\":\"The stated gap is January to April 2024, longer than one quarter, and a Q2 2024 point is plotted.\"}],\"numeric_check\":{\"kind\":\"underdetermined\",\"question\":\"Is the plotted Q2 2024 share in Figure 3 computed from a full quarter or from a partial quarter (May and June only), given the stated gap of January to April 2024?\",\"quantities\":[],\"missing_information\":[\"How the Q2 2024 quarterly share was constructed given the missing April 2024 listing text\",\"The quarterly listing counts and shares underlying Figure 3\"],\"status\":\"unresolved\"},\"suggested_fix\":\"Align the text with the stated gap (January to April 2024) and state whether the Q2 2024 point uses a partial quarter, or flag or drop that point.\"}],\"notes\":[\"numbers_in_text.json was searched by context fields for percent, percentage, % and ratio language and read against the full text; the inventory was not read entry by entry. full_text.md and the page text were read.\",\"Recomputed and found consistent: 70-36=34 unique articles; 5+8+21=34 coded articles; 5/34=14.7% (15%); 34/70=48.6% (49%); Table 3 and Table 4 agreement 33/34=97.1%; Table 2 article counts 4+1+1+1=7 = 5 relevant + 2 planned; Table 6 19+10=29 and 19+10+9+5=43; 266 625+433 954=700 579; Table 8 shares 38.1/61.9/13.4/10.8/10.7/9.8/3.8/1.0 recompute from counts; NVDB geometry registration 4 Sep 2026 to opening 5 Oct 2026 is about one month; Table 5 length 2,132 m against road-link ranges 1492+641=2,133 m is a 1 m rounding-level difference and is not reported.\",\"Table 8 type shares are consistent with Figure 2 word shares within the bounds expected from non-exclusive types (type share at least the largest word share and at most the sum of its listed words); the 20 listed words cover only part of each type, so this is a bounds check only.\",\"Figure 4 county values (Oslo 60.8%, Akershus 52.0%, Telemark 14.4%, Nordland 12.9%, Møre og Romsdal 6.8%) match the rounded text values. The national share of 38% could not be checked against county weights, since county listing counts are not reported.\",\"Not verifiable from retained artifacts: external statistics (60 percent increase in Copenhagen, up to five percentage points in Bergen, 96 percent accuracy in Bartik et al., about 70 percent of housing transactions via FINN.no) and Table 7 keyword counts. Section 6.2 'between a third and a half' is approximate (15 to 24 of 44 is 34 to 55%) and is not reported.\",\"Table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, per the parser-quality guidance; table values were read from page text. The Figure 4 chart image was not viewed, so its dashed national line was not checked visually.\"],\"completion\":{\"version\":1,\"state\":\"complete\",\"scope_description\":\"Numerical audit of the 18-page paper: abstract, introduction, Sections 3 to 8, Tables 1 to 9, Figures 1 to 4 and Appendix A. Central counts, percentages, agreement tables, totals, time spans and adding-up relations were recomputed from page text and retained images.\",\"checks_completed\":[\"Read the parser-quality output and used page text and page images in place of the unreliable table CSV/markdown\",\"Read full_text.md, then searched numbers_in_text.json contexts for percent, percentage-point and ratio language\",\"Recomputed the pilot funnel (70, 36, 34, 5, 8, 21, 2) and its percentages, and tested the 2 of 34 yield sentence against the article-level count\",\"Recomputed the 2x2 agreement tables and the 97% agreement, and compared footnote 3 with Table 3 and the Section 4.1 text\",\"Checked Table 6 date-precision and project totals against the abstract, Section 5 and the conclusion\",\"Checked Table 2 article counts and Table 5 dates, lengths and keys against the text\",\"Recomputed Table 8 totals and shares and tested the non-additivity note and type-share bounds against Figure 2 word shares\",\"Compared Figure 4 county values and Figure 3 endpoints, the 9 percentage point change and the gap period with the text and Appendix A.1\",\"Tested the classification-rule examples in Appendix A.3.2 against Table 9 and Figure 2 colouring\"],\"missing_checks\":[],\"evidence_limitations\":[\"Table CSV/markdown objects were not used because of parser-quality defects; Tables 1, 2 and 5 to 9 were read from page text only\",\"numbers_in_text.json was searched by context and not read entry by entry\",\"Figure 3 values and point positions were read visually and are approximate\",\"The Figure 4 image was not viewed; county shares come from page text\",\"External statistics and the Table 7 keyword counts cannot be recomputed from retained artifacts\",\"The classification order implemented in the SQL or Python code and the construction of the Q2 2024 point in Figure 3 are not in the retained artifacts\"]},\"coverage\":[{\"item_id\":\"assigned_remit\",\"source_object_ids\":[],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read full_text.md and page text, searched numbers_in_text.json contexts for percent, ratio and difference language, and recomputed central counts, shares and time spans.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Four items found and linked to NUM-001 to NUM-004; two are verified numerical defects and two are cannot_verify. All other central figures recomputed or are external and unverifiable. numbers_in_text.json was searched by context and not read entry by entry.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\",\"NUM-002\",\"NUM-003\",\"NUM-004\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"sampled\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read the Figure 1 values (70, 34 at 49%, 5 at 15%, 2) from page 4 text; recomputed 34/70 and 5/34; compared the caption and surrounding text.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Funnel arithmetic is correct. The '2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent)' sentence mixes an openings count with an article denominator (NUM-001).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-001\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Viewed figure_2.png. Compared bar labels with the text (9.8%, about 5% for the next four) and with the Table 8 type shares by bounds, and checked word colour categories against Table 9.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Word shares match the text. Colours for bysykkelstativ and syklende do not follow a literal first-type reading; the effect is unresolved (NUM-003, cannot_verify).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-003\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Viewed figure_3.png. Checked about 35% in 2020, about 44% at the end of the period, the 9 percentage point rise, the 2023 dip and the 2024 gap against the text and Appendix A.1.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Endpoints, rise and dip match; the gap description conflicts with Appendix A.1 and a Q2 2024 point is plotted, with its construction unstated (NUM-004, cannot_verify). Values were read visually and are approximate.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-004\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Compared the page-17 county values with the text's rounded values (61, 52, 38, 14, 13, 7) and checked ordering and the 15-county count.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"County values and rounding are consistent with the text. The chart image and the dashed national line were not viewed, and the 38% national share could not be checked against county weights.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"peripheral\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8ec9459ce44d02c62d0a27bf\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 1 from page 5 text; checked the example quantities (3 km, 3.5 m, 4 articles in 2 newspapers) against Table 2 and Table 5.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Mostly qualitative. The Homborsund '4 articles in 2 newspapers' agrees with Table 2 (4 articles). Physical example values are not tied to a source in the paper.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-dbc6f4a9a830bbbd128e371e\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 2 from page 5 text; summed articles (4+1+1+1=7) against 5 relevant plus 2 planned; checked dates and footnotes against Table 5 and the text.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Counts and dates are consistent with Section 3.1.4 and Table 5. The structured file is truncated, so page text was used.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e3774f186493fe1cf3afe556\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Recomputed row and column totals and the 33/34 = 97.1% agreement; compared the table with the page-7 text and with footnote 3 on page 10.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Table arithmetic is correct. The footnote 3 description of the Stord article conflicts with the table's off-diagonal cell and the text (NUM-002).\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-002\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-a9068469a80185aaa27470fa\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Recomputed Table 4 totals and 33/34 = 97.1%; compared with the text on majority coding, the Stord disagreement and the all-three date match.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Arithmetic and text agree. The 97% rests on 3 relevant articles in a 34-article sample, a limit the authors acknowledge.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-e6d7a21f6dac33af8ecba464\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 5 from page 9 text; checked the one-month gap between 4 Sep and 5 Oct 2026, the road-link ranges against the 2,132 m length (1492+641=2,133), and the municipality and county numbers.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All checks are consistent. The 1 m difference in length is rounding-compatible. The structured file merges columns, so page text was used.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-ff90f28affccf4abf5c4e78c\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 6 from page 10 text; summed 19+10+9+5=43 and 19+10=29; compared with the abstract, Section 5, the conclusion and the 14 of 15 counties statement.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Totals and cross-references agree.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-2c51ead4a14e19e7c3de50a9\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 7 counts from page 11 text; compared with the 44-project base, the 'almost all' location claim (42/44), the 18 ceremony + 26 = 44 split and the 17+2=19 day-dated projects against Table 6.\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"Counts are within the 44-project base and the split sums to 44. 'Between a third and a half' is approximate (15 to 24 of 44 is 34 to 55%) and is not reported. Keyword-based counts cannot be reproduced from retained artifacts.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-8cd1361a5f77a70c5008ee4d\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 8 from page 15 text, not the split CSV columns; recomputed 266 625+433 954 = 700 579 and every share from its count; checked the non-additivity note and the types' sum (346 827 > 266 625).\",\"status\":\"checked_no_issue\",\"reason\":\"All shares recompute from counts to the printed rounding and match the text (38.1%, 13.4%, about 11%). The classification rule behind the type rows is the subject of NUM-003.\",\"finding_ids\":[],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"},{\"item_id\":\"display:OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\",\"source_object_ids\":[\"OBJ-b0c2f2010110ab92e8c28a1c\"],\"claim\":null,\"check_performed\":\"Read Table 9 and the A.3.2 precedence rule from page 18 text; compared word assignments with the rule and with Figure 2 colours.\",\"status\":\"linked_finding\",\"reason\":\"Precedence rule and two assignments conflict on a literal reading (NUM-003, cannot_verify). The effect on Table 8 shares cannot be computed from retained artifacts.\",\"finding_ids\":[\"NUM-003\"],\"attempted\":true,\"importance\":\"central\",\"scope\":\"exhaustive\"}]}","structured_output":{"reviewer":"numerical_auditor","paper_id":"bicycle-infrastructure-paper","run_status":"ok","summary":"Most reported figures recompute: the pilot funnel (70 hits, 36 duplicates, 34 unique), the 2x2 agreement tables (33/34 = 97%), the Table 6 project precision breakdown (19+10+9+5 = 43; 19+10 = 29), the Table 8 listing counts and shares, the Table 8 type shares against Figure 2 word shares (bounds only), and the Figure 4 county values against the text. Two verifiable defects were found. (1) The pilot yield \"2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent)\" uses a count of distinct openings (2) against a count of articles (34), while the paper's own article-level count of articles coded relevant is 5. (2) Footnote 3 says the Stord article was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 shows the second coder with 4 relevant articles against 3 for the pilot coder, and the text identifies the one disagreement article as the Stord article. Two further items cannot be resolved numerically from retained artifacts: whether the Appendix A.3.2 \"first type in the table\" rule is consistent with the bysykkelstativ and syklende assignments in Table 9 and Figure 2 and how this affects Table 8 type shares; and how the plotted Q2 2024 point in Figure 3 was computed, given that the stated gap runs January to April 2024 while the text says only the first quarter is missing. Table CSV/markdown extraction is unreliable per parser-quality guidance, so table numbers were read from page text and retained images.","findings":[{"id":"NUM-001","category":"percentage_denominator_unit_mismatch","finding_summary":"The pilot yield 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place' uses a count of distinct openings (2) as the numerator over a count of articles (34); the paper's own article-level count of articles coded relevant is 5 of 34.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"medium","confidence":"high","location":{"page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Pilot sample","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Figure 1 (page 4) lists 34 unique articles, 5 coded 'relevant' (15% retained) and 2 'Distinct openings that took place'. Section 3.1.4 states 'Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.' (four Homborsund articles and one Stod). The numerator 2 therefore counts projects/openings, while the denominator 34 counts articles. In article units the paper's own count is 5 of 34 (14.7%, shown as 15% in Figure 1), or 3 of 34 (8.8%) after the validation recode of the two pre-opening Homborsund articles (Section 3.1.4). The statement that 2 openings were found is consistent with the data; the article-level share is not. The Figure 1 caption 'Only 2 of 70 search hits concern a cycling infrastructure opening' has the same unit mix, but the caption is not separately numerically assessed here. Whether the sentence is meant to refer to articles or openings is not stated.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 4 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2","text_quote":"Only 2 of the 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 5 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_005.md","page":5,"page_label":"5","section":"3.1.4","text_quote":"Of the five relevant articles, only two unique openings were found.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-9d16c139938370d7a97e77c6","correspondence":"text","verification_note":null},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 4 Figure 1 labels","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_004.md","page":4,"page_label":"4","section":"3.1.2 Figure 1","text_quote":"Coded “relevant” 5 15 % retained","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-1a119a3cb70f2153fc56dd97","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Figure 1 chart labels are retained in the page-4 text; the figure_1.png crop omits the chart, so the page text was used."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"2 of 34 unique articles (about 6 percent) concern an opening that took place","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"The numerator counts openings; the paper's article count coded relevant is 5 (3 after the validation recode)."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"2","source_id":"S1","unit":"articles (as worded in the sentence)","sample":"pilot sample, 34 unique articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Numerator in 'Only 2 of the 34 unique articles'; the same number is the count of distinct openings in Figure 1 and Section 3.1.4","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"5","source_id":"S3","unit":"articles","sample":"pilot sample, 34 unique articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Figure 1 'Coded relevant' count of articles (four Homborsund and one Stod per Section 3.1.4)","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Same 34 unique pilot articles. The 5 counts articles coded relevant; the 2 counts distinct openings that took place. The sentence applies the openings count to an article denominator. The article-level count after the validation recode (3) is stated in Section 3.1.4, but the paper does not say which version the sentence intends.","observed_discrepancy":"Stated numerator 2 'articles' versus 5 articles coded relevant in the same 34-article sample (3 after the validation recode); the stated 6% (2/34 = 5.9%) corresponds to openings, not articles. 5/34 = 14.7%; 3/34 = 8.8%.","possible_explanation":"The authors may have intended an opening-level statement and used the article denominator, or may have intended articles that report an opening that actually took place before the validation recode.","suggested_correction":"State the yield in one unit, either articles (5 of 34, or 3 of 34 after the validation recode, specifying which) or openings (2 distinct openings), and align the Figure 1 caption."},"suggested_fix":"Restate the pilot yield in a single unit (articles or openings) and state which article count (5 or 3) is intended; align the Figure 1 caption."},{"id":"NUM-002","category":"cross_source_count_inconsistency","finding_summary":"Footnote 3 says the Stord article was coded not relevant by both human coders, but Table 3 shows 4 relevant articles for the second coder against 3 for the pilot coder, and the text says the only disagreement article is the Stord article.","issue_type":"manuscript_issue","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6 Further Uses (footnote 3)","text_quote":"was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4)","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The 44 projects include the 43 in Section 5 and the project in Stord, which appears only in the pilot and was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4).","assessment":"no","cannot_verify_reason":null,"evidence_summary":"Table 3 (second coder in columns) has pilot-coder rows 'Relevant 3 0 3' and 'Not relevant 1 30 31', and column totals 'Total 4 30 34'; the pilot coder has 3 relevant articles and the second coder 4. The only off-diagonal cell is pilot coder 'Not relevant' and second coder 'Relevant'. The Section 4.1 text says 'The only article they disagree on covers a dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County'. If the Stord article is that article, one coder coded it relevant, which conflicts with footnote 3 saying both coded it not relevant. The retained text does not say which coder gave which code, nor whether the footnote's Stord project is the same article as the Section 4.1 disagreement article (the Stord article in the disagreement is a dispute article, not an opening article); the check relies on the table cell structure and the text. Table 3 body cells were compared with table_3.png by the parser audit and match.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 10 footnote 3","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_010.md","page":10,"page_label":"10","section":"6","text_quote":"was coded as not relevant by both human coders (Section 4)","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-e9b90e0f75ce05ff1ce150cc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Footnote text is split across two lines in the extraction."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 7 Table 3 totals","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1 / Table 3","text_quote":"Total 4 30 34","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 3 read from page text because the table markdown has a merged header."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 7 text on the disagreement","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4.1","text_quote":"The only article they disagree on covers a","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"The sentence continues on the next line: 'dispute between Stord municipality and Vestland County'."},{"id":"S4","type":"text","label":"page 7 pilot coder relevant count","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_007.md","page":7,"page_label":"7","section":"4","text_quote":"of which 3 were coded as relevant in the pilot","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-4e6da301f188ae5c7e5d0a63","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"A footnote marker is attached to 'pilot' in the extraction and is not part of the quote."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Stord article coded not relevant by both human coders","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3","S4"],"relation":"contradicts","note":"Table 3 gives the second coder one more relevant article than the pilot coder, and the text identifies the one disagreement article as the Stord article."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"cross_source","quantities":[{"value":"3","source_id":"S4","unit":"articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Number of articles the pilot coder coded relevant (Table 3 row 'Relevant 3 0 3')","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"},{"value":"4","source_id":"S2","unit":"articles","sample":"34 unique pilot articles","denominator":"34 unique articles","context":"Number of articles the second coder coded relevant (Table 3 'Total 4 30 34'); 'unclear' counted as not relevant per the Table 3 note","rounding_half_width":"0","scale":"number"}],"comparability":"Both counts refer to the same 34 pilot articles and the same relevance coding. Footnote 3 prints no number; it implies that neither coder coded the Stord article relevant, in which case the second coder's relevant count would not exceed the pilot coder's. That the disagreement article is the Stord article of footnote 3 is taken from the Section 4.1 text.","observed_discrepancy":"The second coder has 4 relevant articles and the pilot coder 3; the one disagreement article is described as the Stord article, whereas footnote 3 says both coders coded the Stord article not relevant.","possible_explanation":"The footnote may refer to a different Stord article or to the pilot coder only, or may reflect a later recode. The retained text does not say.","suggested_correction":"State which coder coded the Stord article as relevant and reconcile footnote 3 with Table 3, or clarify which Stord article the footnote refers to."},"suggested_fix":"Reconcile footnote 3 with Table 3 and the Section 4.1 text, stating which coder (and the LLM) classified the Stord article as relevant."},{"id":"NUM-003","category":"classification_rule_vs_reported_shares","finding_summary":"The Appendix A.3.2 rule 'given the first type in the table' does not obviously produce the bysykkelstativ and syklende assignments shown in the text, Table 9 and Figure 2; whether this changes the Table 8 type shares cannot be computed from retained artifacts.","issue_type":"cannot_verify","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2 Classification of cycling mentions","text_quote":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table. For example: words containing “bysykkel” (city bike), such as “bysykkelstativ”, are counted as infrastructure.","assessment":"cannot_verify","cannot_verify_reason":"The retained artifacts do not contain the implemented classification order or any manual override, nor listing-level overlaps between words, so the effect of the apparent rule conflict on the Table 8 type shares cannot be computed.","evidence_summary":"Table 9 orders the types 'The word “bicycle”', Proximity, Parking & storage, Leisure, Infrastructure, Other. 'Parking & storage' includes 'stativ' (rack), so 'bysykkelstativ' contains a Parking & storage part that precedes Infrastructure, yet the text says it is counted as infrastructure and Figure 2 colours bysykkelstativ (0.5%) blue (Infrastructure), while sykkelstativ (1.2%) is orange (Parking & storage). 'syklende' (0.3%) is listed under Infrastructure and coloured blue although it contains 'sykle', a Proximity part listed earlier. The example for bysykkel may be an explicit override rather than a literal first-type outcome, which the text does not say. Table 8 reports listing-level any-word type shares, so the effect of reclassifying one or two words (each at most 0.5% and 0.3% of listings) cannot be derived from the retained evidence. The Table 8 type shares are within the bounds implied by Figure 2 word shares.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 18 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_018.md","page":18,"page_label":"18","section":"A.3.2","text_quote":"If a word fits more than one type, it is given the first type in the table.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-03dcf11e0f4853cb90843dbe","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 9 rows read from page text because table_9.md is unstructured per parser quality."},{"id":"S2","type":"figure","label":"figure_2.png","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_2.png","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 2","text_quote":null,"url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-be07133eb1a3ae76638fe011","correspondence":"visual","verification_note":"Figure 2 viewed. Bars for bysykkelstativ (0.5%) and syklende (0.3%) are in the Infrastructure colour; sykkelstativ is in the Parking & storage colour; sykle is in the Proximity colour."},{"id":"S3","type":"text","label":"page 15 Table 8 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md","page":15,"page_label":"15","section":"A.2 / Table 8","text_quote":"Infrastructure 93 786 13.4%","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Table 8 read from page text, not the split CSV columns."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"First-type rule determines the type of each word","source_object_ids":["S1","S2"],"relation":"partial","note":"Two assignments do not follow a literal reading of the stated precedence."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Do the reported Table 8 type shares (for example Infrastructure 13.4% of 700 579 listings) follow the stated first-type rule, or would reclassifying bysykkelstativ and syklende change them?","quantities":[{"value":"13.4","source_id":"S3","unit":"percent of all listings","sample":"700 579 FINN.no listings, January 2020 to October 2026","denominator":"700 579 listings","context":"Table 8 Infrastructure share, quoted for context only; no recomputation of the type shares under an alternative classification is possible","rounding_half_width":"0.05","scale":"percent"}],"missing_information":["Listing-level overlap between words, since a listing can contain several word types","The classification order actually implemented and any manual overrides"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"State the actual precedence or the override applied (for example whether 'bysykkel' words are classified before 'stativ'), and confirm that Table 8 and Figure 2 use the same assignment."},{"id":"NUM-004","category":"timing_gap_inconsistency","finding_summary":"The text says only the first quarter of 2024 is missing, but the stated data gap is January to April 2024, which reaches into Q2, and Figure 3 plots a Q2 2024 point without saying how it was computed.","issue_type":"cannot_verify","severity":"low","confidence":"medium","location":{"page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 3","text_quote":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","precision":"exact"},"claim_text":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","assessment":"cannot_verify","cannot_verify_reason":"The retained artifacts do not state how the Q2 2024 point in Figure 3 was constructed (partial quarter, only May and June listings, or another treatment), and the underlying quarterly series is not available, so the effect of the partial gap on the plotted share cannot be assessed.","evidence_summary":"Appendix A.1 states 'Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data' and the Figure 3 caption says 'missing listing text from January to April 2024'. Four months extends one month beyond Q1. The page-16 sentence says only the first quarter is missing. In the Figure 3 image the last pre-gap point sits at about 2023.75 (Q4 2023, about 34%) and the first post-gap point (about 39%) at about 2024.25, so a Q2 2024 point is plotted. If April is missing, that point may rest on May and June only and may not be comparable with full-quarter points; the text does not say. The text's rise from about 35 percent to about 44 percent is consistent with the plotted endpoints.","source_objects":[{"id":"S1","type":"text","label":"page 16 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_016.md","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2","text_quote":"The first quarter of 2024 is missing due to the gap in the listing text data.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-8f4894d007c8a183053537bc","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Sentence is split across two lines in the extraction."},{"id":"S2","type":"text","label":"page 15 text","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/pages/page_015.md","page":15,"page_label":"15","section":"A.1","text_quote":"Listings from January to April 2024 are missing due to a gap in the listing text data.","url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-6402cd90a906f1f82672a86f","correspondence":"text","verification_note":"Sentence is split across two lines in the extraction."},{"id":"S3","type":"figure","label":"figure_3.png","path":"work/bicycle-infrastructure-paper/parsed/figures/figure_3.png","page":16,"page_label":"16","section":"A.2 / Figure 3","text_quote":null,"url":null,"object_id":"OBJ-22f18338a427285653860df1","correspondence":"visual","verification_note":"Figure 3 viewed. No point between about 2023.75 and about 2024.25; the first post-gap point sits at about 2024.25 (Q2 2024). Point positions and values are read visually and are approximate."}],"claim_evidence_links":[{"claim_text":"Only the first quarter of 2024 is missing","source_object_ids":["S1","S2","S3"],"relation":"partial","note":"The stated gap is January to April 2024, longer than one quarter, and a Q2 2024 point is plotted."}],"numeric_check":{"kind":"underdetermined","question":"Is the plotted Q2 2024 share in Figure 3 computed from a full quarter or from a partial quarter (May and June only), given the stated gap of January to April 2024?","quantities":[],"missing_information":["How the Q2 2024 quarterly share was constructed given the missing April 2024 listing text","The quarterly listing counts and shares underlying Figure 3"],"status":"unresolved"},"suggested_fix":"Align the text with the stated gap (January to April 2024) and state whether the Q2 2024 point uses a partial quarter, or flag or drop that point."}],"notes":["numbers_in_text.json was searched by context fields for percent, percentage, % and ratio language and read against the full text; the inventory was not read entry by entry. full_text.md and the page text were read.","Recomputed and found consistent: 70-36=34 unique articles; 5+8+21=34 coded articles; 5/34=14.7% (15%); 34/70=48.6% (49%); Table 3 and Table 4 agreement 33/34=97.1%; Table 2 article counts 4+1+1+1=7 = 5 relevant + 2 planned; Table 6 19+10=29 and 19+10+9+5=43; 266 625+433 954=700 579; Table 8 shares 38.1/61.9/13.4/10.8/10.7/9.8/3.8/1.0 recompute from counts; NVDB geometry registration 4 Sep 2026 to opening 5 Oct 2026 is about one month; Table 5 length 2,132 m against road-link ranges 1492+641=2,133 m is a 1 m rounding-level difference and is not reported.","Table 8 type shares are consistent with Figure 2 word shares within the bounds expected from non-exclusive types (type share at least the largest word share and at most the sum of its listed words); the 20 listed words cover only part of each type, so this is a bounds check only.","Figure 4 county values (Oslo 60.8%, Akershus 52.0%, Telemark 14.4%, Nordland 12.9%, Møre og Romsdal 6.8%) match the rounded text values. The national share of 38% could not be checked against county weights, since county listing counts are not reported.","Not verifiable from retained artifacts: external statistics (60 percent increase in Copenhagen, up to five percentage points in Bergen, 96 percent accuracy in Bartik et al., about 70 percent of housing transactions via FINN.no) and Table 7 keyword counts. Section 6.2 'between a third and a half' is approximate (15 to 24 of 44 is 34 to 55%) and is not reported.","Table CSV/markdown was not used as primary evidence, per the parser-quality guidance; table values were read from page text. The Figure 4 chart image was not viewed, so its dashed national line was not checked visually."],"completion":{"version":1,"state":"complete","scope_description":"Numerical audit of the 18-page paper: abstract, introduction, Sections 3 to 8, Tables 1 to 9, Figures 1 to 4 and Appendix A. Central counts, percentages, agreement tables, totals, time spans and adding-up relations were recomputed from page text and retained images.","checks_completed":["Read the parser-quality output and used page text and page images in place of the unreliable table CSV/markdown","Read full_text.md, then searched numbers_in_text.json contexts for percent, percentage-point and ratio language","Recomputed the pilot funnel (70, 36, 34, 5, 8, 21, 2) and its percentages, and tested the 2 of 34 yield sentence against the article-level count","Recomputed the 2x2 agreement tables and the 97% agreement, and compared footnote 3 with Table 3 and the Section 4.1 text","Checked Table 6 date-precision and project totals against the abstract, Section 5 and the conclusion","Checked Table 2 article counts and Table 5 dates, lengths and keys against the text","Recomputed Table 8 totals and shares and tested the non-additivity note and type-share bounds against Figure 2 word shares","Compared Figure 4 county values and Figure 3 endpoints, the 9 percentage point change and the gap period with the text and Appendix A.1","Tested the classification-rule examples in Appendix A.3.2 against Table 9 and Figure 2 colouring"],"missing_checks":[],"evidence_limitations":["Table CSV/markdown objects were not used because of parser-quality defects; Tables 1, 2 and 5 to 9 were read from page text only","numbers_in_text.json was searched by context and not read entry by entry","Figure 3 values and point positions were read visually and are approximate","The Figure 4 image was not viewed; county shares come from page text","External statistics and the Table 7 keyword counts cannot be recomputed from retained artifacts","The classification order implemented in the SQL or Python code and the construction of the Q2 2024 point in Figure 3 are not in the retained artifacts"]},"coverage":[{"item_id":"assigned_remit","source_object_ids":[],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Read full_text.md and page text, searched numbers_in_text.json contexts for percent, ratio and difference language, and recomputed central counts, shares and time spans.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Four items found and linked to NUM-001 to NUM-004; two are verified numerical defects and two are cannot_verify. All other central figures recomputed or are external and unverifiable. numbers_in_text.json was searched by context and not read entry by entry.","finding_ids":["NUM-001","NUM-002","NUM-003","NUM-004"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"sampled"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce","source_object_ids":["OBJ-0b391e5449c5ec2c409159ce"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Read the Figure 1 values (70, 34 at 49%, 5 at 15%, 2) from page 4 text; recomputed 34/70 and 5/34; compared the caption and surrounding text.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Funnel arithmetic is correct. The '2 of 34 articles (about 6 percent)' sentence mixes an openings count with an article denominator (NUM-001).","finding_ids":["NUM-001"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa","source_object_ids":["OBJ-95ecd7ea3c5b8d724f48fffa"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Viewed figure_2.png. Compared bar labels with the text (9.8%, about 5% for the next four) and with the Table 8 type shares by bounds, and checked word colour categories against Table 9.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Word shares match the text. Colours for bysykkelstativ and syklende do not follow a literal first-type reading; the effect is unresolved (NUM-003, cannot_verify).","finding_ids":["NUM-003"],"attempted":true,"importance":"central","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798","source_object_ids":["OBJ-7414d59aee2e3ad29a820798"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Viewed figure_3.png. Checked about 35% in 2020, about 44% at the end of the period, the 9 percentage point rise, the 2023 dip and the 2024 gap against the text and Appendix A.1.","status":"linked_finding","reason":"Endpoints, rise and dip match; the gap description conflicts with Appendix A.1 and a Q2 2024 point is plotted, with its construction unstated (NUM-004, cannot_verify). Values were read visually and are approximate.","finding_ids":["NUM-004"],"attempted":true,"importance":"peripheral","scope":"exhaustive"},{"item_id":"display:OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5","source_object_ids":["OBJ-d491066348ee1a73c8bce8f5"],"claim":null,"check_performed":"Compared the page-17 county values with the text's rounded values (61, 52, 38, 14, 13, 7) and checked ordering and the 15-county count.","status":"checked_no_issue","reason":"County values and rounding are consistent with the text. The chart image and the dashed national line were not viewed, and the 38% national share could not be checked against county weights.","finding_ids":[],"attempted":true,"importance":"peripheral","scope":"exhaust